abstract: >-
  karpos-downscaling provides Python tools for downscaling atmospheric
  reanalyses (ERA5, CERRA) to kilometer-scale resolution, conditioned on
  digital elevation models and calibrated against sparse in-situ sensor
  networks (Sencrop). The package supports three families of methods behind
  a single configuration: statistical (lapse-rate + quantile mapping + RBF
  Sencrop), deep learning (U-Net with FiLM conditioning), and foundation
  models (Prithvi WxC fine-tuning). Applications include the derivation of
  parametric agricultural insurance indices for frost, extreme precipitation,
  wind, and heat. The methodology supports stratification by synoptic regime
  for interpretable performance reporting.
